    {
      "id": "17bbbbbad7d5610e22f7bafd35052b270f7367e7",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2585749597,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This essentially undoes c84681aca2fb1144df94880d9997a5800006c2e0 by @stigbjorlykke (plus adds support for using the `&amp;` entity, which I'm not entirely sure is necessary considering that it's not rich text and won't be interpreted as such, and I don't understand why you would expect that to work.)\n\nSo I presume that he had some reason for disallowing mnemonics in plugin menus in the first place, possibly because most people wouldn't intend them, or wouldn't be familiar with them. The change does seem to be after the GTK UI went away, but it is worth noting that the use of mnemonics and doubled ampersand is not toolkit independent.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-26T00:43:08.039Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-26T00:43:08.039Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 393591829,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20335,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a2366847ffe920d3670c185e5091212312528711",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2585892150,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I checked that change from Stig and the comment says\n\n_An ampersand in the menu item or a button is used as shortcut, so use \"&&\" to get a real ampersand._\n\nI am not sure what exactly he wanted to achieve there and it was 5 years ago.\n\nShorcuts are everywhere in the menu and it seems those work fine. Those are properly handled by `QAction()`.\n\nUsing shortcuts from plugin would be equivalent to those menu items to me (also handled by `QAction()`) so I am not sure the \"not toolkit independent\" concern is valid (Qt shall handle these properly).\n\nAbout `&amp;`, you have a valid point since rich text should not be considered here.\n\nShortcuts for menu items added via an external plugin can be useful and valuable the same way shortcuts for the current menu items.",
          "author": {
            "id": 20971927,
            "username": "rtommy",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tamas Regos",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/20971927/avatar.png?v=1788090511",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rtommy"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-26T03:44:23.094Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-26T03:44:23.094Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 393591829,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20335,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "681ba223a95891addc358092e8ee1cabf5cb3b60",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2585968776,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Using shortcuts from plugin would be equivalent to those menu items to me (also handled by QAction()) so I am not sure the \"not toolkit independent\" concern is valid (Qt shall handle these properly).\n\nWhat you are proposing is that the Title, as entered in Lua, for example, have a double ampersand to have a single ampersand displayed, and a single ampersand not be displayed but used as a mnemonic. That's putting Qt behavior into the Lua plugin source.\n\nWhen there was the GTK front end, a double ampersand in the title entered in the Lua code would be displayed as a double ampersand in the GTK front end. The current behavior essentially removes the Qt-specific special handling of ampersands as a way to automatically set up a shortcut.\n\nWith your patch, there would be no way to have a single Lua plugin that would have the same title appearance on both toolkits (unlike with the current source.) But, again, the only GUI frontend at the moment is Qt, which is what makes the concern not relevant.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-26T04:56:07.987Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-26T04:57:12.514Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 393591829,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20335,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a8f0ca6e59add34d3b9f7c47180ab91f0a1d6c2d",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2585988874,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I see your point.\n\nYes, this patch means putting Qt behavior into the Lua plugin source. Indeed.\n\nThe current \"old\" code was most likely working just fine with GTK front end but it does not work with Qt the same way. I understand.\n\nSo what you said, the only GUI frontend at the moment is Qt. Therefore, should not we align the code to actually support (consider) Qt and not GTK?\n\nSo what are proposing? \n\nLeave it as it is or since the only GUI frontend at the moment is Qt, we should change the code?",
          "author": {
            "id": 20971927,
            "username": "rtommy",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tamas Regos",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/20971927/avatar.png?v=1788090511",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rtommy"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-26T05:10:26.982Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-26T05:10:26.982Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 393591829,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20335,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
